# Testing

Full evaluation model (pyramid, mocks, staging, Playwright plan): `README.md` §11 and `docs/agents/adrs/ADR-009-web-functional-e2e.md`.

## Backend (pytest)
- `httpx.AsyncClient` + `ASGITransport` against `app.main:app`
- Test auth, RBAC, happy path per router
- `AI_PROVIDER=mock` — no network in tests
- Email/payments/storage stay on mock/local defaults in CI

## Frontend (Jest + RTL)
- Colocate under `__tests__/`
- Test behavior, not implementation

## Web browser e2e (not implemented — S-010)
- Do not add Cypress/Selenium
- Playwright (Python) per ADR-009 / TP-S-010 when that slice is built
- Run against Compose or staging with mock vendors, never live LLM/payment keys

## Mobile (Flutter)
- `flutter analyze` + `flutter test` (unit/widget, `mobile/test/`) — no device needed; enforced by
  `.githooks/pre-commit` when any `mobile/` path is staged
- `flutter drive` (real Android emulator, `mobile/integration_test/`) — CI only; this machine has no Android SDK, don't attempt it locally
- Full when-what-runs table with if/else reasoning: `ANDROID_APP_STRATEGY.md` § "Testing & CI flow"

## Before merge
- `cd backend && pytest`
- `cd frontend && npm test`
- `cd mobile && flutter analyze && flutter test`

## Local git hooks (every commit, IDE included)
- One-time: `git config core.hooksPath .githooks`
- Hook refuses commits on `main`/`master` — use `git checkout -b feature/…` then PR
- Hook runs Cursor↔Claude sync check; if `mobile/` staged, runs `flutter analyze && flutter test`
- Emulator stays CI-only; do not add it to the local hook

## CI/CD — speed optimizations never skip a check, they only change *when* it runs
- Cheap checks (lint/unit) run on every push, never cancelled.
- Expensive checks (emulator integration) cancel a *stale* run when a newer commit supersedes it on the same PR — the check still always validates the latest commit, never skips it.
- Manual `workflow_dispatch` exists as an on-demand full-validation override for critical fixes.
- **Known gap:** backend/frontend app-test workflows are currently dispatch-only (PR triggers commented). `main` has no branch-protection rule requiring CI to pass, and Railway's deploy is not gated on CI status. See `README.md` §11 and `ANDROID_APP_STRATEGY.md`.
